{#-
  Solutions on a problem page (HANDOFF §6.4 SolutionCard; board
  Problem-A.dc.html, phone Problem-Phone.dc.html; SPEC §7.2, §7.5).

    {% from "problem/solutions.njk" import solutionsSection %}
    {% set tiers = solutions | solutionsByTier(videos, worksheets) %}
    {% set ratingsOn = site.features.ratings === true %}
    {% set feedbackOn = site.features.feedback === true %}
    {% if tiers.main.length %}{{ solutionsSection('main', tiers.main, ratingsOn, feedbackOn) }}{% endif %}
    {% if tiers.extra.length %}{{ solutionsSection('extra', tiers.extra, ratingsOn, feedbackOn) }}{% endif %}

  solutionsSection(tier, items, ratings, feedback)
    tier     'main' ("Main solutions", #main-solutions) or 'extra' ("Other
             things that can help", #more-solutions). The page omits a
             section with no items: the extra one when there are no extras,
             and both on a stand-alone problem (SPEC §7.2).
    items    tiers.main or tiers.extra from `solutionsByTier`; with none,
             the macro renders nothing (no heading without cards)
    ratings  exactly true (the layout passes site.features.ratings ===
             true): each open card's row of controls ends with the ratings
             widget (SPEC §12, partials/rating.njk)
    feedback exactly true (the layout passes site.features.feedback ===
             true): each open card's row of controls has the video's
             "Feedback" button (SPEC §13)

  solutionCard(solution, ratings, feedback): one card, an <li> in the
  grid.

  The closed card (V1, project lead, 2026-11-09) is the same on every card:
  the thumbnail band with its play disc, step chip ("1 Main" / "1 Extra")
  and duration, then the title and the description (the solution's blurb,
  or the video's description where it has none: `solution.description`,
  SPEC §7.2). Nothing else: no quick "Handout" link and no rating summary.
  Below 600px it is the Problem-Phone accordion row (number disc, title,
  description, chevron).

  The open card is the video template (partials/video-block.njk), as every
  video on the site is: the step chip with Close at its right, the title
  (h3) and the description, the video, then "Audio only", "Handout",
  "Feedback" and "Was this helpful?".

  Worksheets (SPEC §7.6; project lead, 2026-11-13: "Add a section to
  expanded solution video boxes where worksheets can go"). After the
  template, and so under its row of controls and across the card, an open
  card lists its video's worksheets: `solution.worksheets`, the video's
  rows of data/worksheets.csv in the file's order (`solutionsByTier`). They
  belong to the video, so a video shows the same worksheets on every
  problem where it is a solution. The video template itself doesn't change
  and knows nothing of them: only a solution card adds this section, never
  the problem's own video or a Start here chapter.
    <section class="worksheets">, a region named by its heading;
    <h4>     "Worksheet" for one and "Worksheets" for several, then the
             video's title for screen readers (the card's title is the
             template's <h3>); id solution-<video_id>-worksheets;
    <ul>     one link per worksheet, styled as the row's "Handout"
             (.format-button, the download icon): its title, with " (PDF)"
             for screen readers, to /media/worksheets/<file>.
             data-worksheet holds the worksheet_id.
  A video with no worksheets has no section at all (no empty heading). The
  links are plain links, so they work without JavaScript. Styles:
  src/css/pages/problem.css ("Solution card: open").

  Without JavaScript each card is a native <details name="solution">: the
  <summary> is the closed card, and opening it shows the video, its row of
  controls and its worksheets, while the <summary> stays above them as the
  card's name and only close control (the template's header ships `hidden`,
  so there the worksheets' <h4> follows the section's <h2>). The shared
  `name` keeps one card open at a time across both sections where browsers
  support it; elsewhere several can be open, which is harmless. Cards start
  closed, so the first screen holds one video facade, not two; add `open`
  to a card's <details> to start it open, and src/js/solutions.js keeps it
  open.

  src/js/solutions.js turns each <details> into a <div>, its summary into an
  <h3> holding a <button aria-expanded aria-controls>, and the panel into a
  region labelled by the template's title. It shows the template's header
  (step chip, Close, title, description); while a card is open its face is
  hidden at every width, and Close closes it. Opening a card closes any
  other, in either section, pausing its media, and moves focus to its title.

  ids (unique per page; the validator allows each video once per page):
  solution-<video_id> on the card, plus -panel, -blurb, -length and
  -worksheets, and the template's video-<video_id>-title.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
{%- from "partials/step-chip.njk" import stepChip -%}
{%- from "partials/video-block.njk" import videoBlock -%}

{%- macro solutionCard(solution, ratings=false, feedback=false) -%}
{%- set video = solution.video -%}
{%- set id = 'solution-' + video.video_id -%}
{%- set label = 'Main' if solution.tier == 'main' else 'Extra' -%}
{%- set spoken = video.duration | spokenDuration -%}
{%- set ratingsOn = ratings === true -%}
{%- set feedbackOn = feedback === true -%}
{%- set sheets = solution.worksheets or [] -%}
<li class="solution solution--{{ solution.tier }}" id="{{ id }}">
  <details class="solution__disclosure" name="solution">
    <summary class="solution__face"><span class="solution__face-inner">
      <span class="solution__band" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- if video.thumbnail %}<img class="solution__thumb" src="/media/thumbs/{{ video.thumbnail }}" alt="" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async">{% endif %}
        <span class="play-disc play-disc--sm">{{ icon('play', 20) }}</span>
        {{ stepChip(solution.n, label, variant='sm paper') }}
        <span class="duration-badge solution__duration">{{ video.duration }}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="solution__disc" aria-hidden="true">{{ solution.n }}</span>
      <span class="solution__text">
        <span class="solution__title">{{ video.title }}</span>
        <span class="solution__blurb" id="{{ id }}-blurb">{{ solution.description }}</span>
        <span class="solution__length visually-hidden" id="{{ id }}-length">Video{% if spoken %}, {{ spoken }}{% endif %}</span>
      </span>
      <span class="solution__chevron" aria-hidden="true">{{ icon('chevron-down', 18) }}</span>
    </span></summary>
    <div class="solution__panel" id="{{ id }}-panel">
      {{ videoBlock(video, heading=3, description=solution.description, label={ num: solution.n, text: label }, close=id + '-panel', bleed='card', ratings=ratingsOn, feedback=feedbackOn) }}
      {%- if sheets.length %}
      <section class="worksheets" aria-labelledby="{{ id }}-worksheets">
        <h4 class="worksheets__title" id="{{ id }}-worksheets">Worksheet{{ 's' if sheets.length != 1 }}<span class="visually-hidden">: {{ video.title }}</span></h4>
        <ul class="worksheets__list" role="list">
          {%- for sheet in sheets %}
          <li><a class="format-button" href="/media/worksheets/{{ sheet.file }}" type="application/pdf" data-worksheet="{{ sheet.worksheet_id }}">{{ icon('download', 18, 'format-button__icon') }}{{ sheet.title }}<span class="visually-hidden"> (PDF)</span></a></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </section>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </details>
</li>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro solutionsSection(tier, items, ratings=false, feedback=false) -%}
{%- if items and items.length -%}
{%- if tier == 'main' -%}
  {%- set sectionId = 'main-solutions' -%}
  {%- set eyebrow = 'Things to try' -%}
  {%- set heading = 'Main solutions' -%}
  {%- set intro = 'Most people start here. Pick the one that sounds most doable for you.' -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- set sectionId = 'more-solutions' -%}
  {%- set eyebrow = 'If you want more' -%}
  {%- set heading = 'Other things that can help' -%}
  {%- set intro = 'Useful extras, or for when the main ideas aren’t quite enough.' -%}
{%- endif %}
<section class="solutions solutions--{{ tier }}" id="{{ sectionId }}" aria-labelledby="{{ sectionId }}-title">
  <div class="solutions__head">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow solutions__eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading" id="{{ sectionId }}-title">{{ heading }}</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="solutions__intro">{{ intro }}</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="solution-grid" role="list">
    {%- for solution in items %}
    {{ solutionCard(solution, ratings, feedback) }}
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
